# Markdown features

Inline styles combine freely: **bold**, *italic*, `code`, struck, **struck bold** and [a struck link](https://example.com), and styles glued inside one word like **un***believ*`able`.

## Task list

- [x] Completed item
- [ ] Pending item
  - [x] Nested completed item
  - [ ] Nested pending item
- A plain bullet for comparison

## Image

Local images are resolved relative to this file; the title becomes a caption.

![](images/img-001.png)

*Figure 1 — a generated diagram*

A missing image falls back to its alt text and a warning:

*\[image: a picture that is not there\]*

## Footnotes

A statement with a footnote.1 Another one,2 and the first again.1

## Raw HTML

A `<br>` tag breaks the line, other tags like \<kbd>this\</kbd> stay literal, and comments are dropped.

```
<div class="note">
  Block HTML is shown verbatim, never interpreted.
</div>
```

Prices in dollars such as $5 or $10 stay as written, and so does math source like $E = mc^2$.

---

1. Supporting information, shown as an endnote.
2. Footnotes are numbered in the order they are first referenced.
